Culinary use
{{See also|Typha latifolia#Uses}}
Several parts of the plant are edible, including during various seasons the dormant sprouts on roots and bases of leaves, the inner core of the stalk, green bloom spikes, ripe pollen, and starchy roots. It can be prepared in the same way as Typha latifolia. The edible stem is called {{Lang|vi|bồn bồn}} in Vietnam.photo
